-Regional experiments also provide practical models for follow up studies. In soil crusts associated with \textit{Rhazya stricta}, biomass increased threefold within a week of watering \cite{aslam2016rainfall}, consistent with the early response windown selected by our rainfall models. In Jizan and AlWahbah, host-resolved surveys found the strongest plant-associated differntiation in the root endosphere \cite{eida2018desertplants}. Our root-adjacent compartment, which differed from bulk soil and had the lowest alpha diversity, represents the soil end of this root--soil gradient. Post-rainfall sampling and comparisons among identified host plants would connect these regional observations.
