 \subsection*{Conclusions}
 
 The Empty Quarter hosts a structured microbial landscape. Bacterial
-assemblages change across the west to east, mainly through turnover of genera, and compartments differ in composition and alpha diversity within sites. Climate, soil pH, and soil chemical composition covary with the geographic pattern, and predicted metabolic potential also follows the same geographic and compartment structure. Exploratory rainfall models identify the first days after rain as a window for event-based sampling. Together, the survey provides a regional baseline and specific hypothesis on geographic, plant-associated, and metabolic patterns for repeated surveys and experiments.
