 \subsubsection*{Alpha diversity (within-sample)}\label{sec:alpha_methods}
-We summarized within-sample diversity using three measures. We calculated Shannon diversity ($H$) with natural logarithms at full read depths as it is less sensitive to variation \cite{shirazi2021revisiting}. We also estimated rarefied richness as Hulbert's expected number of species as it controls for variation in sequencing depth \cite{hurlbert1971nonconcept} at $25{,}000$ reads ($E[S_{25k}]$) near the $5$th percentile of library size (median $382{,}432$ reads per sample). This allowed us to retain $95\,\%$ of the samples, and the rest were omitted from richness comparisons. To measure abundance relative to rarefied richness, we used a normalized Shannon index $H/\log(E[S_{25k}])$ (Supplementary Section~\ref{sup:alphadiversity}).
