-\textbf{Compartment contrasts.} To separate the effect of compartment from differences among sites and campaigns, we compared surface, shallow subsurface, and root-adjacent soil with paired, site-level differences in a repeated measures design that removes within-site and within-campaign variation. For each compartment contrast, we used only the sites and campaigns for which we had samples, averaged the differences within campaign, then averaged across campaigns within each site. We obtained confidence intervals by site-level bootstrap and tested the paired differences with the Wilcoxon signed-rank test, controlling the false discovery rate separately for the Shannon and normalized Shannon comparisons. To confirm that sequencing depth and DNA extraction protocol did not drive the differences, we refitted the contrasts with Gaussian generalized estimating equations (GEEs) that accounted for repeated sampling of the same site (Supplementary Section~\ref{sup:alphadiversity_compartments}, \ref{sup:alphadiversity_confounds}).
