-\textbf{Climate associations.} We tested whether within-site diversity varied with weather and climate measurements. Correlations with our field weather measurements did not remain after correction for multiple testing, so we conducted the remaining analyses with external long-term climate datasets (Section~\ref{sec:envmeasurements}). We averaged each diversity index within site and used Spearman's correlation with 49-month means of temperature, rainfall, and humidity. We corrected the resulting tests as one family with Benjamini-Hochberg correction, and derived intervals by paired-site bootstrap resampling. Because the three climate summaries are themselves ordered along the sampling transect, we interpret these correlations as descriptions of the environmental axis along which diversity changes, rather than a means of identifying a causal driver (Supplementary Section~\ref{sup:alphadiversity_climate}).
