-\textbf{Short-term rainfall.} To test whether samples collected soon after rainfall were more diverse, we modeled alpha diversity measures as a function of time-dependent cumulative rainfall over the 60 days preceding collection under a rise-and-decay distributed lag kernel (Supplementary Section~\ref{sup:rainfall_kernel}). Because the lag was unknown, we fitted this model across lags from 0.5 to 30 days for each diversity index, adjusting for site, compartment, campaign, and transect position. We repeated this analysis with two independent rainfall datasets (Section~\ref{sec:envmeasurements}). Since selecting the lag with the strongest effect inflates significance, we assessed the whole search against a randomization null that preserves the amount and spatial pattern of rainfall. We estimated the selected effect by refitting the full model on site-level bootstrap resamples. Detailed methods are described in Supplementary Section~\ref{sup:rainfall}.
