-\textbf{Transect model (Redundancy analysis).} To test whether community composition changed across the study transect, we first removed campaign and compartment effects by subtracting from each profile the mean CLR profile of its campaign $\times$ compartment combination (mean taken across sites), and averaged the centred profiles to a single profile per site. The transect coordinate was defined as the first principal component (PC1) of site coordinates in kilometers, oriented from west to east. We related composition of site profiles to linear and quadratic transect terms by redundancy analysis (RDA) \cite{legendre2012rda} and summarized the fit as variance explained, with a delete-one-site jackknife interval with $999$ site permutations (Supplementary Section~\ref{sup:beta_transect}). Since the residuals remained spatially autocorrelated (multivariate Moran's $I$, 5-nearest neighbor graph), we treat the variance explained as descriptive and report its sensitivity to spatially correlated errors (Supplementary Section~\ref{sup:beta_spatialerrors}). We also compared site-level CLR of each genus with the transect coordinate ($200$ tests, Benjamini--Hochberg).
